  "hindi": "हे सोम और पूषन्, तुम दोनों धनों के जनक हो, द्युलोक के जनक हो, पृथिवी के जनक हो; उत्पन्न हुए तुम दोनों को, जो सम्पूर्ण भुवन के रक्षक हैं, देवों ने अमृत की नाभि बनाया।",
  "english": "O Soma and Pūṣan, begetters of riches, begetters of heaven, begetters of earth: born, you two guardians of the whole world, the gods made you the navel of immortality.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Somāpūṣaṇā taken as vocative dual; it could also be nominative. jātau gopau are taken as two accusatives in apposition (the two, born, as guardians) with nābhim a second predicate object of akṛṇvan; the syntax of pāda b is loose.",
