  "hindi": "वे इन दोनों देवों को उत्पन्न होते समय अपनाते हैं; ये दोनों अप्रिय अन्धकारों को छिपा दें। इन दोनों से, सोम और पूषन् के साथ, इन्द्र ने कच्चियों के भीतर पके को उत्पन्न किया, गौओं में।",
  "english": "They delight in these two gods as they are born; may these two hide the unwelcome darknesses. With these two, with Soma and Pūṣan, Indra generated the ripe within the raw ones, in the cows.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "juṣante is 3 pl. with no expressed subject; the sense \"they welcome these two gods as they are born\" is the most natural, but the subject is not stated. gūhatām read as 3 du. imperative (\"let them hide\"); an injunctive/past sense is possible. In pāda b pakvam and āmāsu are neuter/feminine adjectives with no noun expressed; usriyāsu is \"in the (bright) cows\". The common understanding that ripe milk is meant is not stated in the verse and is not translated.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.040.2a",
   "002.040.2b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
