  "hindi": "एक ने द्युलोक में ऊँचा आसन बनाया है, दूसरे ने पृथिवी पर, अन्तरिक्ष में। वे दोनों हमारे लिए बहुत वांछित, बहुत समृद्ध, धन की वृद्धि को, नाभि को, हमारे भीतर खोल दें।",
  "english": "One has made his seat high up in heaven, the other on the earth, in the atmosphere. May those two release for us the much desired, abounding increase of wealth, the navel, in us.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The token \"di̱vya1nyaḥ\" carries a printed accent digit (1); the Devanagari reads divy anyaḥ. Two gods, three places: the distribution of heaven, earth and atmosphere between the two is not clear, and adhy antarikṣe may go with pṛthivyām (earth and the atmosphere above). vi ṣyatām is vi + √so (syatām, with ṣ by sandhi). nābhim and its relation to the other accusatives is unclear.",
